a52sxq: ICE legacy mode + native inline crypto for standard (raw) keys (opt-in)

The 6.12 Qualcomm ufshcd-crypto-qti advertises only HW-wrapped keys and the yupik DT sets
qcom,ice-use-hwkm, while the A52s ROMs use standard keys (fstab: aes-256-xts v2+inlinecrypt_optimized,
metadata via dm-default-key, no wrappedkey): every /data bio went through blk-crypto-fallback (CPU AES).
qcom_ice.a52_no_hwkm=1 keeps ICE in legacy mode; ufshcd_crypto_qti.a52_raw_keys=1 then advertises
BLK_CRYPTO_KEY_TYPE_STANDARD and programs raw keys with qcom_ice_program_key (SCM ice_set_key, the
upstream ufs-qcom path). qcom_ice_program_key_hwkm() returns 0 for a raw key without programming it, so
the profile must never claim standard keys on that path. Both default 0. In legacy mode the evict uses the matching qcom_scm_ice_invalidate_key. (2026-11-21)

